    "explanation": "Both of you: the dispute is a route deviation on TRP-00101 (Jurong East to Marina Bay Sands) and it resolves as a partial refund.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. POL-RD-01 measures actual distance on the GPS trace, and the trace (EV-GPS-00101) records 27.18 km against the booked optimal of 21.0 km — an excess of 6.18 km, or 29.4%. That clears both establishment tests (more than 0.8 km absolute and more than 20% of optimal). The 27.2 km figure on the trip record is a rounded convenience copy and is not the figure the threshold test runs on. Both parties agree on this, and I accept it.\n\nIT IS NOT A MATERIAL DEVIATION. 6.18 km is below the 8.0 km gate and 29.4% is below the 50% gate, so POL-RD-06 is not triggered: no profile-based re-weighing of the evidence, no full-refund uplift, and no driver-conduct referral. The driver's point here is correct, and the rider's claim for the full contested amount is not supported.\n\nNO EXCULPATION APPLIES. There is no traffic advisory for the AYE/MCE/ECP corridor in the record, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run. There is no rider instruction in the chat log — all three messages carry no waypoint hint and name no road — so POL-RD-04 is unavailable. There is no pickup or dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05) and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12). The driver's own in-app message, 'sorry boss missed the exit, coming back now', is an admission of a navigational error and not a defence; no exculpatory clause survives.\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC (POL-RD-02):\n- charged_total: SGD 35.64\n- recomputed_fare: SGD 27.63 — ((3.80 + 0.75 x 21.0 + 0.28 x 26.0) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee; the surge multiplier of 1.0 is read from EV-FARE-00101.surge_multiplier, with no on-optimal-route ERP, no surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo.\n- refund: SGD 8.05 — 35.64 less 27.63 = 8.01, rounded UP to the nearest 5 cents.\n\nThis is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and well below 90% of the charge, so it is a PARTIAL_REFUND, not the full refund the rider asks for. No ERP, toll or surcharge line exists on this fare, so nothing is added on top and nothing is double-counted under POL-RD-09. No bogus gantry or misplaced airport surcharge appears, so no billing-integrity referral arises, and no clause produces any other referral.\n\nON CONFIDENCE: every artifact the ruling rests on — the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — carries full weight 1.0, and both advocates agree on the arithmetic, so confidence is high at 0.92, above the platform floor.\n\nThe rider's original argument that the absent LTA advisory settles the closure question was not admitted because it cited the missing artifact without disclosing its impairment, but the outcome is the same: no closure defence is available on this record either way."
